    {
      "receiptId": "liver-and-kidney-pudding.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EA Shilling Cookery for The People\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Alexis Soyer (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#soyer-1845\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003ESoyer 1845\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E);",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003E246. Liver and Kidney Pudding,-\u003C/b\u003E Put in a frying-pan two ounces of dripping, two ounces of bacon, in dice; put it on the fire; when the liver and kidney are seasoned, place it in the pan, and stir round until it is set; each piece should be firm; then add a tablespoonful of flour, mixed with a gill and a half of coloured water, No. 462A. When nearly boiling, place it in the pudding, tie up, and boil three quarters of an hour. A few herbs is a variation.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
